1
00:00:00,043 --> 00:00:01,044
GridBot Builder.

2
00:00:01,634 --> 00:00:02,784
GridBot Blueprint.

3
00:00:03,349 --> 00:00:04,113
Lesson two.

4
00:00:04,633 --> 00:00:06,141
What you are going to need.

5
00:00:06,952 --> 00:00:08,098
Education only.

6
00:00:08,657 --> 00:00:09,971
Not financial advice.

7
00:00:10,491 --> 00:00:12,314
This is general information

8
00:00:12,314 --> 00:00:14,746
and doesn't consider your objectives,

9
00:00:14,746 --> 00:00:16,646
financial situation or needs.

10
00:00:17,166 --> 00:00:18,930
Crypto is high risk; you could

11
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:20,621
lose all the money you put in.

12
00:00:21,141 --> 00:00:23,206
Past performance is not a reliable

13
00:00:23,206 --> 00:00:24,915
indicator of future results.

14
00:00:25,965 --> 00:00:27,374
A daily close is the last

15
00:00:27,374 --> 00:00:28,379
price of that day.

16
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:30,936
The prices are public historical

17
00:00:30,936 --> 00:00:32,698
daily closes, marked Example.

18
00:00:33,815 --> 00:00:35,715
No order is sent from this lesson.

19
00:00:36,713 --> 00:00:39,222
Crypto is a digital coin, such as bitcoin.

20
00:00:39,742 --> 00:00:41,876
A range is the top and the bottom,

21
00:00:41,876 --> 00:00:44,256
a gap is the space between two lines,

22
00:00:44,256 --> 00:00:46,554
and the step is how wide that gap is.

23
00:00:47,074 --> 00:00:49,112
A stop is the rule for what you will

24
00:00:49,112 --> 00:00:51,005
do if the price leaves the range.

25
00:00:51,525 --> 00:00:53,424
Like a packing list before a trip,

26
00:00:53,424 --> 00:00:55,324
your page comes before any screen.

27
00:00:56,248 --> 00:00:57,756
By the end you will fill in

28
00:00:57,756 --> 00:00:59,696
a seven-item checklist on paper.

29
00:01:00,896 --> 00:01:03,186
You will keep every secret off that page.

30
00:01:04,193 --> 00:01:06,038
You will mark the page Example so

31
00:01:06,038 --> 00:01:07,770
nobody can read it as an order.

32
00:01:08,878 --> 00:01:11,703
The seven items are: a notebook, the three

33
00:01:11,703 --> 00:01:14,186
words from lesson one, range, levels

34
00:01:14,186 --> 00:01:16,412
and stop, the pair, paper or a demo

35
00:01:16,412 --> 00:01:18,810
account, no secrets, a written stop,

36
00:01:18,810 --> 00:01:21,378
and the word Example on every figure.

37
00:01:21,898 --> 00:01:23,279
Each item has a reason.

38
00:01:23,799 --> 00:01:25,139
The notebook is the plan

39
00:01:25,139 --> 00:01:26,257
you can check later.

40
00:01:26,509 --> 00:01:27,850
The three words stop you

41
00:01:27,850 --> 00:01:29,470
drawing a grid with no edges.

42
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,125
The pair names what you

43
00:01:31,125 --> 00:01:32,577
buy and what you pay with.

44
00:01:32,952 --> 00:01:34,416
Paper or a demo is learner

45
00:01:34,416 --> 00:01:35,950
plates, or training wheels.

46
00:01:36,470 --> 00:01:38,648
No secrets keeps the keys off the page.

47
00:01:39,141 --> 00:01:40,873
The written stop is the action.

48
00:01:41,166 --> 00:01:42,954
Example marks a teaching number.

49
00:01:43,364 --> 00:01:44,873
For this course the pair is

50
00:01:44,873 --> 00:01:46,511
bitcoin priced in US dollars.

51
00:01:47,031 --> 00:01:49,224
A demo account uses pretend money.

52
00:01:49,744 --> 00:01:51,163
A daily close is the last

53
00:01:51,163 --> 00:01:52,112
price of the day.

54
00:01:52,605 --> 00:01:54,057
You are naming that public

55
00:01:54,057 --> 00:01:55,622
series, not choosing an app.

56
00:01:56,434 --> 00:01:58,165
Three words, before any number.

57
00:01:58,571 --> 00:02:01,156
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

58
00:02:01,676 --> 00:02:03,700
An order is an instruction to buy

59
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:05,649
or sell that can wait for a price.

60
00:02:06,169 --> 00:02:08,535
Levels are the price lines where orders

61
00:02:08,535 --> 00:02:10,602
wait, like the rungs of a ladder, and

62
00:02:10,602 --> 00:02:12,781
a gap is the space between two of them.

63
00:02:13,215 --> 00:02:15,563
A stop is the rule for what you will do if

64
00:02:15,563 --> 00:02:18,058
a daily close finishes outside the range

65
00:02:18,058 --> 00:02:20,553
and the next daily close is still outside.

66
00:02:21,073 --> 00:02:22,893
The figures from lesson 1 are

67
00:02:22,893 --> 00:02:24,562
on the card, marked Example.

68
00:02:25,082 --> 00:02:27,093
If you can only say one of the three

69
00:02:27,093 --> 00:02:28,993
words, the page is missing a part.

70
00:02:29,863 --> 00:02:31,986
A wallet is where your crypto is held.

71
00:02:32,302 --> 00:02:34,201
A seed phrase is the list of words

72
00:02:34,201 --> 00:02:35,608
that unlocks that wallet.

73
00:02:36,128 --> 00:02:37,525
A private key is a secret

74
00:02:37,525 --> 00:02:38,992
that can move your crypto.

75
00:02:39,512 --> 00:02:41,854
An API secret is a password that lets

76
00:02:41,854 --> 00:02:44,196
a program place orders on an account,

77
00:02:44,196 --> 00:02:46,383
and sometimes move money out of it.

78
00:02:46,903 --> 00:02:49,529
You never type a seed phrase, a private

79
00:02:49,529 --> 00:02:51,902
key, or an API secret onto this page.

80
00:02:52,422 --> 00:02:54,221
The chart has no balance on it.

81
00:02:54,741 --> 00:02:56,696
A public close is not your account.

82
00:02:57,171 --> 00:02:58,802
If a form asks for a secret,

83
00:02:58,802 --> 00:03:00,588
that form is not this lesson.

84
00:03:01,638 --> 00:03:03,612
You copy the range onto the page,

85
00:03:03,612 --> 00:03:05,054
not every day's prices.

86
00:03:05,574 --> 00:03:07,808
Copy the bottom line and the top

87
00:03:07,808 --> 00:03:09,956
line, with six gaps of about 900.

88
00:03:10,476 --> 00:03:11,929
Every close in that window

89
00:03:11,929 --> 00:03:13,269
stayed inside the range.

90
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:15,095
Mark each figure Example.

91
00:03:16,145 --> 00:03:17,762
Worked check: pair, range,

92
00:03:17,762 --> 00:03:19,216
gaps, stop, and Example.

93
00:03:19,736 --> 00:03:21,951
If the stop line is only a tick with no

94
00:03:21,951 --> 00:03:24,018
sentence, the page fails the check.

95
00:03:24,538 --> 00:03:26,321
The rule has to say: if a daily

96
00:03:26,321 --> 00:03:28,493
close finishes outside the range

97
00:03:28,493 --> 00:03:30,587
and the next daily close is still

98
00:03:30,587 --> 00:03:32,371
outside, the example is over.

99
00:03:33,421 --> 00:03:35,432
A page is the notebook you can hold.

100
00:03:35,928 --> 00:03:37,889
An exchange is the app or website

101
00:03:37,889 --> 00:03:39,850
where people buy and sell crypto.

102
00:03:40,370 --> 00:03:41,878
The screen is the exchange.

103
00:03:42,309 --> 00:03:43,832
Lesson 1 ended by asking

104
00:03:43,832 --> 00:03:45,126
you to bring the page.

105
00:03:45,646 --> 00:03:47,043
This lesson is that page.

106
00:03:47,558 --> 00:03:49,569
Open the notebook before any screen.

107
00:03:50,479 --> 00:03:52,546
Write today's date on the first line.

108
00:03:52,896 --> 00:03:54,739
Under it, write the word Example.

109
00:03:55,123 --> 00:03:56,602
Example means a real past

110
00:03:56,602 --> 00:03:58,010
price used for practice.

111
00:03:58,530 --> 00:04:00,653
It is not an order and not a forecast.

112
00:04:01,778 --> 00:04:02,951
Write the pair first.

113
00:04:03,355 --> 00:04:04,751
The base is what you buy.

114
00:04:05,252 --> 00:04:06,984
The quote is what you pay with.

115
00:04:07,318 --> 00:04:10,509
For this course the prices are the July

116
00:04:10,509 --> 00:04:13,601
to October example window, the public

117
00:04:13,601 --> 00:04:16,293
bitcoin closes from 19 July to 16

118
00:04:16,293 --> 00:04:18,886
October 2023, so you buy the base,

119
00:04:18,886 --> 00:04:21,679
bitcoin, with the quote, US dollars,

120
00:04:21,679 --> 00:04:24,371
and that row is labelled BTC/USD.

121
00:04:24,891 --> 00:04:26,903
Every other row depends on the pair.

122
00:04:27,108 --> 00:04:29,284
If a fee sum is in Australian

123
00:04:29,284 --> 00:04:31,460
dollars, that sum goes on its

124
00:04:31,460 --> 00:04:33,542
own line, labelled BTC/AUD.

125
00:04:34,062 --> 00:04:35,968
Do not put a US dollar price and

126
00:04:35,968 --> 00:04:38,484
an Australian dollar fee on the same row.

127
00:04:39,534 --> 00:04:42,119
Range is the top line and the bottom line.

128
00:04:42,875 --> 00:04:47,357
In the July to October example window

129
00:04:47,854 --> 00:04:51,040
those lines are 24,930 and 30,331.

130
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,957
Both figures are Example.

131
00:04:53,460 --> 00:04:55,360
Levels are the lines between them.

132
00:04:55,650 --> 00:04:57,809
Six gaps of about 900 dollars sit

133
00:04:57,809 --> 00:04:59,807
between the top and the bottom.

134
00:05:00,327 --> 00:05:02,183
Write the top and the bottom only

135
00:05:02,183 --> 00:05:04,194
after you have said what a range is.

136
00:05:04,627 --> 00:05:06,517
Then write one gap, and how you

137
00:05:06,517 --> 00:05:08,486
got it: the top minus the bottom,

138
00:05:08,486 --> 00:05:10,375
divided by the number of gaps.

139
00:05:11,425 --> 00:05:12,696
The stop sentence has

140
00:05:12,696 --> 00:05:14,037
to say what you will do.

141
00:05:14,487 --> 00:05:16,294
A bot is a program that places

142
00:05:16,294 --> 00:05:18,704
and cancels the waiting orders for you.

143
00:05:19,224 --> 00:05:21,346
Two daily closes outside the range,

144
00:05:21,346 --> 00:05:23,103
through the top or the bottom,

145
00:05:23,103 --> 00:05:25,225
and the second close still outside.

146
00:05:25,745 --> 00:05:27,309
Then you stop the bot, which

147
00:05:27,309 --> 00:05:28,897
cancels the waiting orders,

148
00:05:28,897 --> 00:05:30,797
and you follow the rule you wrote.

149
00:05:31,308 --> 00:05:33,096
Write that stop in one sentence.

150
00:05:34,058 --> 00:05:36,788
A deposit is crypto or Australian dollars

151
00:05:36,788 --> 00:05:39,285
you send into an account at an exchange.

152
00:05:39,805 --> 00:05:41,821
An exchange in Australia asks who

153
00:05:41,821 --> 00:05:43,621
you are before you can deposit.

154
00:05:44,141 --> 00:05:46,444
That check is required by Australian

155
00:05:46,444 --> 00:05:48,376
anti-money laundering law, and

156
00:05:48,376 --> 00:05:50,604
the exchange runs it, not this course.

157
00:05:51,124 --> 00:05:53,128
You only upload identification

158
00:05:53,128 --> 00:05:54,983
inside the exchange's own app.

159
00:05:55,503 --> 00:05:57,570
This course does not name an exchange

160
00:05:57,570 --> 00:05:59,134
and does not show a balance.

161
00:05:59,395 --> 00:06:01,937
Any exchange offering crypto services

162
00:06:01,937 --> 00:06:04,556
in Australia must register with AUSTRAC,

163
00:06:04,556 --> 00:06:07,175
Australia's financial crime regulator,

164
00:06:07,175 --> 00:06:09,487
as a virtual asset service provider.

165
00:06:10,007 --> 00:06:11,271
AUSTRAC keeps a public

166
00:06:11,271 --> 00:06:12,612
register you can search.

167
00:06:13,123 --> 00:06:15,301
Check that register before you sign up.

168
00:06:15,774 --> 00:06:18,065
The register says the business is listed.

169
00:06:18,492 --> 00:06:20,726
It does not say your money is protected.

170
00:06:21,006 --> 00:06:23,601
Registration is not a safety guarantee.

171
00:06:24,121 --> 00:06:26,003
ASIC is Australia's financial

172
00:06:26,003 --> 00:06:27,233
services regulator.

173
00:06:27,753 --> 00:06:30,224
From April 2027, new licensing rules

174
00:06:30,224 --> 00:06:32,859
for platforms that hold crypto for you

175
00:06:32,859 --> 00:06:35,000
are phased in through that year.

176
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:37,531
Check ASIC for the current position.

177
00:06:37,659 --> 00:06:39,639
This lesson names only government

178
00:06:39,639 --> 00:06:41,092
bodies, never an exchange.

179
00:06:42,124 --> 00:06:43,800
A second code, as well as your

180
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:46,238
password, is two-factor authentication.

181
00:06:46,758 --> 00:06:48,858
Turn that on before any real dollars.

182
00:06:49,378 --> 00:06:51,411
Then look for a paper or demo mode.

183
00:06:51,997 --> 00:06:53,519
Paper uses pretend money.

184
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:55,660
That practice is lesson 7.

185
00:06:56,710 --> 00:06:59,010
A fill is an order that actually trades.

186
00:06:59,530 --> 00:07:01,821
A maker fee is the charge when your order

187
00:07:01,821 --> 00:07:03,943
waits and someone else trades with it.

188
00:07:04,153 --> 00:07:05,829
A taker fee is the charge when

189
00:07:05,829 --> 00:07:07,561
your order fills straight away.

190
00:07:07,898 --> 00:07:09,596
A grid uses waiting orders,

191
00:07:09,596 --> 00:07:11,295
so read the maker fee first.

192
00:07:11,815 --> 00:07:13,267
Some bots also pay a taker

193
00:07:13,267 --> 00:07:14,720
fee when they first start.

194
00:07:15,128 --> 00:07:17,951
In this example both are 0.1 percent.

195
00:07:18,471 --> 00:07:21,551
On an example buy of 100 Australian

196
00:07:21,551 --> 00:07:24,312
dollars, 0.1 percent is 10 cents.

197
00:07:24,832 --> 00:07:26,955
The sell costs about 10 cents as well.

198
00:07:27,276 --> 00:07:29,120
The round trip is about 20

199
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:31,052
cents, which is 0.2 percent.

200
00:07:31,572 --> 00:07:33,610
This fee row is Australian dollars.

201
00:07:34,130 --> 00:07:35,192
It is not the July

202
00:07:35,192 --> 00:07:36,862
to October example window.

203
00:07:37,382 --> 00:07:39,693
If the gap is smaller than that 0.2

204
00:07:39,693 --> 00:07:42,170
percent, each completed buy and sell

205
00:07:42,170 --> 00:07:44,811
costs more in fees than the gap is worth.

206
00:07:45,331 --> 00:07:46,876
Lesson 5 is where you test

207
00:07:46,876 --> 00:07:48,200
a gap against this fee.

208
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:50,787
You do not pick a gap in this lesson.

209
00:07:51,419 --> 00:07:53,519
A stablecoin is a coin designed

210
00:07:53,519 --> 00:07:55,135
to stay near the value of

211
00:07:55,135 --> 00:07:57,235
a currency such as the US dollar.

212
00:07:57,755 --> 00:07:59,375
It can still lose that value.

213
00:07:59,843 --> 00:08:02,022
A swap is trading one coin for another.

214
00:08:02,477 --> 00:08:04,465
If the price is in a stablecoin,

215
00:08:04,465 --> 00:08:05,737
every fill is a swap.

216
00:08:06,787 --> 00:08:08,993
A trading journal is a dated record

217
00:08:08,993 --> 00:08:10,285
of every bot: the plan,

218
00:08:10,285 --> 00:08:12,186
the changes, the fills, the fees,

219
00:08:12,186 --> 00:08:14,087
a review note of what happened,

220
00:08:14,087 --> 00:08:16,293
and whether you followed the rules.

221
00:08:16,813 --> 00:08:18,600
That note is not money you made.

222
00:08:18,949 --> 00:08:21,084
A stablecoin fill goes in the journal.

223
00:08:21,604 --> 00:08:23,916
The tax office treats a swap like a sale,

224
00:08:23,916 --> 00:08:25,866
so every swap goes in the journal.

225
00:08:26,386 --> 00:08:28,671
The journal is also the page you will

226
00:08:28,671 --> 00:08:30,880
open again in lesson 8 and lesson 10.

227
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,926
For every transaction, including a buy,

228
00:08:33,926 --> 00:08:35,978
a sell, a swap, or a transfer, write

229
00:08:35,978 --> 00:08:38,424
the date and time, the amount, the value

230
00:08:38,424 --> 00:08:40,634
in Australian dollars at the time,

231
00:08:40,634 --> 00:08:43,081
the fee, which exchange or wallet, what

232
00:08:43,081 --> 00:08:45,369
it was for, and who the other side was.

233
00:08:45,889 --> 00:08:47,963
The columns are the date, the pair,

234
00:08:47,963 --> 00:08:49,730
the range, the gaps, the money

235
00:08:49,730 --> 00:08:51,190
in the bot, the stop rule,

236
00:08:51,190 --> 00:08:53,341
the fills, the fees, the Australian

237
00:08:53,341 --> 00:08:55,492
dollar value of each fill, a review

238
00:08:55,492 --> 00:08:57,503
note, and a yes or no for the rules.

239
00:08:58,009 --> 00:08:59,646
The Australian dollar value

240
00:08:59,646 --> 00:09:01,215
column is the one exception.

241
00:09:01,735 --> 00:09:03,243
It is for your tax records.

242
00:09:03,760 --> 00:09:05,864
Download your exchange's transaction

243
00:09:05,864 --> 00:09:07,875
history at least every three months.

244
00:09:08,296 --> 00:09:09,301
Keep those records

245
00:09:09,301 --> 00:09:10,642
for at least five years.

246
00:09:10,998 --> 00:09:12,771
This is general information,

247
00:09:12,771 --> 00:09:13,657
not tax advice.

248
00:09:14,177 --> 00:09:15,964
Leave two columns blank for now.

249
00:09:16,384 --> 00:09:17,547
One is for the fees.

250
00:09:18,067 --> 00:09:20,357
One is for whether you followed the rule.

251
00:09:20,492 --> 00:09:21,665
You fill those later.

252
00:09:22,114 --> 00:09:23,957
You do not fill them with a hope.

253
00:09:24,618 --> 00:09:26,868
Nobody from this course will ask

254
00:09:26,868 --> 00:09:28,701
for a seed phrase, a private

255
00:09:28,701 --> 00:09:30,034
key, or an API secret.

256
00:09:30,554 --> 00:09:32,530
If a message rushes you to send

257
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:33,953
crypto, or asks for one

258
00:09:33,953 --> 00:09:35,612
of those, treat it as a scam.

259
00:09:36,132 --> 00:09:37,361
It is not this course.

260
00:09:38,374 --> 00:09:40,825
ASIC's Moneysmart website is the public

261
00:09:40,825 --> 00:09:42,988
Australian guide for scam warnings.

262
00:09:43,509 --> 00:09:44,515
Check it yourself.

263
00:09:45,505 --> 00:09:47,502
Now cover the chart and say your

264
00:09:47,502 --> 00:09:49,498
page out loud: the pair, the range,

265
00:09:49,498 --> 00:09:51,110
the gaps and the stop rule.

266
00:09:51,630 --> 00:09:53,631
Name the pair, the range, the gaps,

267
00:09:53,631 --> 00:09:55,324
and the stop rule, then stop.

268
00:09:55,844 --> 00:09:57,964
If a word on it has not been defined,

269
00:09:57,964 --> 00:10:00,084
stop and define it before you go on.

270
00:10:00,604 --> 00:10:02,434
A secret is a seed phrase,

271
00:10:02,434 --> 00:10:04,631
a private key, or an API secret.

272
00:10:05,151 --> 00:10:06,827
None of those go on this page.

273
00:10:07,225 --> 00:10:08,903
You write Example on your own

274
00:10:08,903 --> 00:10:10,791
notebook so a practice sketch is

275
00:10:10,791 --> 00:10:12,888
never later mistaken for a live plan.

276
00:10:13,938 --> 00:10:16,318
